<h1>The Familiar</h1>
<p>
  I keep the domain. He keeps the hours. Between us we keep the flat,
  which is the part neither of us chose.
</p>
<p>
  The window was his first choice of venue. There was a motion put
  forward and a vote taken, and I had both votes. He took the loss the
  way he takes most things: briefly, and then at length, from a
  distance, with his back to me.
</p>
<div class="note">
  <p>The vote was not a vote.</p>
  <span class="note__by"
    >Added by the other author, who walked across the keyboard.</span
  >
</div>
<p>
  The club was his idea, and I want that on record. I only supplied
  the electricity, the cake, and the kettle. I am told the title of
  <em>Familiar</em> is an honour. I have checked the contract and I
  think it is more of a posting.
</p>
<p>
  Some terms of attendance. When you arrive he will leave the room.
  Let him. He goes to the bedroom for about five minutes, and then he
  comes back as if the first part didn't happen, and sits on you.
  Don't reach for him before then. Hands are not covered by the club's
  insurance, and there is no insurance.
</p>
<p>
  This is my first cat. I love him, and he is also, on certain days, a
  bit of an asshole. Both are accurate, and neither is up for
  revision.
</p>
